      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That\u2019s Correct!\n\nThe coins in the bag are Bronze, Bronze, Silver,
        and Gold. Since we are drawing one coin, each coin has an equal chance of
        being selected.\n\nLet\u2019s list the possible outcomes:\n\nBronze\u2081,
        Bronze\u2082, Silver, Gold\n\nThere are 4 total possible outcomes. Out of
        these, 1 outcome is a gold coin.\n\nWe can calculate the probability using
        the formula:\n\nP(Gold) = \\frac{\\text{Number of gold coins}}{\\text{Total
        number of coins}}\n\nP(Gold) = \\frac{1}{4}\n\nSo, the probability of drawing
        a gold coin is 1/4 or 0.25 (25%).\n\nThe bag contains 1 gold coin out of
        4 total coins, so the chance of drawing a gold coin is one-fourth."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
