      propertyPath: m_AnchoredPosition.x
      value: 23.5
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 707731474542828200, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_AnchoredPosition.y
      value: -40
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Size
      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 847925133356509755, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That\u2019s Correct!\r\n\r\nThe coins in the bag are Bronze, Bronze,
        Silver, and Gold. Since we are drawing one coin, each coin has an equal chance
        of being selected.\r\n\r\nLet\u2019s list the possible outcomes:\r\n\r\nBronze\u2081,
        Bronze\u2082, Silver, Gold\r\n\r\nThere are 4 total possible outcomes.\r\n\r\nOut
        of these, 2 outcomes are bronze coins.\r\n\r\nWe can calculate the probability
        using the formula:\r\n\r\nP(Bronze) = \\frac{\\text{Number of bronze coins}}{\\text{Total
        number of coins}}\r\n\r\nP(Bronze) = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}\r\n\r\nSo,
        the probability of drawing a bronze coin is 1/2 or 0.5 (50%).\r\n\r\nThe
        bag contains 2 bronze coins out of 4 total coins, so the chance of drawing
        a bronze coin is one-half.\r\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1659184101071729672, guid: 6ca5b3bf0b1bcab46aa5604ec797bce7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_AnchorMax.y
